WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.530
Every Scout troop dreams big.

2
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:06.290
Summer camp, new tents, maybe even a trip
to Alaska.

3
00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:08.370
But those adventures come with a price tag,

4
00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:11.110
and monthly dues don't always cover everything.

5
00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.810
That's where fundraising comes in.

6
00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:16.210
Many councils team up with Trail's End

7
00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:17.930
for the annual popcorn sale.

8
00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:19.930
It's more than just selling snacks.

9
00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:22.450
It's a hands-on way for Scouts to learn
goal-setting,

10
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:23.970
communication, and teamwork,

11
00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.370
all while funding their entire year of Scouting.

12
00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.130
Fundraising isn't just asking for money.

13
00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.050
Scouts sell products like popcorn,

14
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.690
wreaths, or car wash tickets,

15
00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:35.930
so buyers get something they value.

16
00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:39.250
The Trail's End app even makes transactions
safe and cash-free,

17
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:40.810
so you can sell from the couch.

18
00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.970
A great fundraiser starts with a plan.

19
00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:47.130
Units should check their activity calendar,

20
00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:49.770
set a budget, and get approval from the
local council

21
00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:52.210
using a unit money-earning application.

22
00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:53.850
This keeps everything above board

23
00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.530
and focused on the troop's goals.

24
00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:59.410
Popcorn is popular, but it's not the only way.

25
00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.890
Troops across the country run pancake
breakfasts,

26
00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:04.250
car washes, and holiday wreath sales.

27
00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.490
Local businesses often donate supplies,

28
00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:08.410
which means more profit for the unit

29
00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:10.130
and a stronger community connection.

30
00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.850
A successful popcorn sale can fund a whole year

31
00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:16.370
of amazing Scouting.

32
00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:18.210
We're talking summer camp fees,

33
00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.170
leadership training like Wood Badge,

34
00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:23.530
and even once-in-a-lifetime trips to the
National Jamboree.

35
00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.290
It turns a simple snack into real adventure.

36
00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:29.690
Ready to fuel your Scout's next adventure?

37
00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:32.850
Reach out to your local council to learn
about popcorn sales

38
00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:35.050
and other fundraising opportunities in
your area.

39
00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:37.050
Then visit the Trail's End Portal

40
00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.050
to get your unit set up and start selling.
